{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcomes of each lottery, defined as the outcomes with the minimum probability. For Lottery A, the least probable outcome is -3000 Euros with a probability of 0.2%. For Lottery B, the least probable outcome is -6000 Euros with a probability of 0.1%. The reason compares these least probable outcomes and prefers the lottery with the more favorable (i.e., less negative) such outcome. Since -3000 Euros is more favorable than -6000 Euros, the reason would prefer Lottery A. Thus, the decision reason can be applied to this decision problem, and it supports choosing Lottery A.",
